text.en:
Act Numbered Seventeen, entitled "An Act for the reorganization of the Mining Bureau," is
hereby amended to read as follows:
"Section 1. The following employees are hereby authorized for the Mining Bureau:
"(a) A chief of the Mining Bureau, who shall receive compensation at the rate of three
thousand dollars per year;
"(b) A mining engineer and assayer, who shall receive compensation at the rate of one
thousand eight hundred dollars per year;
"(c) A stenographer and typewriter, who shall receive compensation at the rate of one
thousand two hundred dollars per year;
"(d) A translator, who shall receive compensation at the rate of one thousand dollars per
"(e) A draftsman, who shall receive compensation at the rate of four hundred and eighty
dollars per year;
"(f) A draftsman, who shall receive compensation at the rate of three hundred dollars per
"(g) One clerk, Class C;
"(h) One clerk, Class D;
"(i) One clerk, Class I;
"(j) One janitor, at a compensation of one hundred and twenty dollars per year;
"(k) One laborer, at a compensation of eighty dollars per year."
